WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.760
[This is our journey]

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.420
[To 1 million subscribers]

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.640
How it all started

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.080
I think what many of our viewers

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.520
also don't know

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.220
seven years ago when we made our first video

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.900
it was actually on a
channel called EditingSports

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.040
Emil wanted to try out his editing skills

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.080
I had got like an interest

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.920
to do some editing on videos

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.500
So the first video

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.220
it was only me and Emil

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.160
we were filming our training session

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.240
we were doing all sorts of fun trick shots

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.120
Emil was trying out a lot of things

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.560
with all sorts of effects...

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.180
It...

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.960
It was very interesting

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.960
you can say the first video

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.660
it became quite evident

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.400
that people were more impressed by the

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.600
actual tricks

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.860
than my editing skills

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.560
So...

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:00.400
yeah...

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.660
I think it didn't take many videos

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.060
when I started to leave out those special effects

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.700
and we were actually more focusing on the tricks themselves

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.680
We realised that it was the trick shots
people liked

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.180
so

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.020
we did another one

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.820
and that's where Otto came in for the first
time

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.780
I was impressed by the editing

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.580
editing of the videos but

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.380
the tricks weren't so good

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.680
so I figured I had to jump in

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.360
and show Sensei skills

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.300
Me and Emil we played in the same club

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.320
when we we're juniors

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.680
and Otto he was from

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.620
a different city

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.360
but we have also known

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.780
known Otto for a long time

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.400
Our first viral video

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.300
was the ping pong

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.800
estwinglisher?

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.400
extinguisher

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.180
exting

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.100
tinguisher?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.300
Extinguisher

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.140
The candle...

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.200
The candle shot!

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.560
Shutting down the candle

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.040
Before 100k

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.340
our biggest focus was on

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.740
the challenge Pongfinity series

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.220
This is the series where you challenge us

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.860
with your craziest ideas related to table tennis

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.140
which is a super nice way to interact

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.560
with the audience

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.220
You get crazy ideas

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.320
Some of them are absolutely ridiculous

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.880
We get so much inspiration and ideas
from the comments

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.440
Some of them are actually really difficult to pull off

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:53.800
even for us

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.460
I think the fact that we all play table tennis at high level

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.560
really makes it possible for us to

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.420
do some of the challenges we get

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.500
I think it was 2018

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.500
That's when we
started to make videos almost weekly

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.940
Before that it was...

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.000
We had no plan

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.700
we were just... whenever we felt like it

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.820
We posted a video.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.660
Which was not very often

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.080
Then we were thinking that let's give this channel a chance

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.700
And let's see where it takes us.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.900
When we reached 100k subscribers

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.680
It was really massive for us

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:57.440
We never really thought we could possibly reach 100,000 subscribers

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.940
It felt really good and special

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.720
And like we achieved something big

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.200
That really was a big thing for us

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.860
We made a really special video for that

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.840
And the idea was to play

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.600
One rally with 100 different items

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.380
We knew that it's going to be hard

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.840
First of all to find a hundred items

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.260
And bring them to the hall

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.320
And then.. Yeah filming it was...

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.500
It was a nightmare.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.340
It took so long!

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.600
It wasn't really fun

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.320
There were a few tries

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.080
Where we messed up
at like 90+ items

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.040
We had only three items left!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.960
And because it took so long to organize the things

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.700
So after every attempt it took at least 15 minutes

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.200
to get everything back on the table

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.780
And then when it was the last shot...

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.680
The racket cover was on the table and...

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.840
The ball dropped on the racket cover

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.300
We thought that we missed it

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:04.980
We thought:

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.320
"No! That was 99 and we have ruined it!"

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.360
We thought it was 99 but it was actually
hundred

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.600
In the end we got it

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:15.880
It was only

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.040
Just over a year ago when we
hit 100,000.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.740
So it has been really fast

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:22.080
Yeah, it's crazy!

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.520
It's insane to think about it...

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.900
The goal for 2019

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.440
was to hit 1 million

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.760
We had about 230,000

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:35.640
So it was a long way to 1 million

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.980
We mentioned in one of our videos in the beginning of 2019 that:

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.840
Don't forget to subscribe

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.940
to help us reach 1 million subscribers

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:47.420
Yeah to be honest it was quite ambitious

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.440
Then we hit 300K

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.680
And it was time for mine and Miikka's one set showdown

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.140
We had a lot of requests

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.200
To see us playing against each other

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.920
because we hadn't shown that in a video yet

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.720
So that was the first match

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.520
As you know

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.720
I lost that one

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.640
But I have to say it was on purpose

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:22.560
So that Miikka would accept the challenge for the 500K

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:23.920
So I lost this one

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.300
but I'm sure I'll beat you in a best-of-seven

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.140
Yeah I won that set

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.760
And that set the challenge for the 500K big match

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.720
And to make things a bit more
interesting

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.540
If Otto loses

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:37.820
I will cut his beard

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:38.860
And if I loose

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.840
He will get to shave my head

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.260
I think he wouldn't have

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.440
accepted it if I would have won him

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.140
so I had to lose on purpose

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.800
I can always lose one set to Miikka

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.540
We hadn't done that sort of stuff before

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.260
Sort of scetches and comedy stuff

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.140
So we had been postponing the idea for some time

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.140
But then we eventually got the courage

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:16.480
To try out something totally different and something totally new

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.520
We were not quite sure how it would work out

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.140
But it was really fun to film

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.740
You really need to get out of your comfort zone and

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.400
Do something special

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.800
For example screaming

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.920
I can't do this

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.860
I'm not really a screamer

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:39.700
Ready?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.760
I'm not ready.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.500
I need some water

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:44.520
Hit me.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.960
I remember it was a super fun video to film

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.160
And we were laughing all the
time when we were filming the video

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:07.900
We had a really fun idea to do the
intros in different languages

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.720
It was fun at first

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.940
Everybody obviously wanted us to do

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:19.120
our intro in your language

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.980
So the comment-section was literally flooded

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.120
With comments that:

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.620
Do the intro in German

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.720
Do the intro in Polish

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.140
Do the intro in my language

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.080
And we stopped getting
actual challenge requests!

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.360
Everything was just about the language
intros

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.560
So we thought - Okay this has to stop!

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.200
We have to stop doing this

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.000
Now the comment-section has calmed down

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.680
And we are getting good challenge ideas again

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.960
Then came 500K and the big match

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.860
Between me and Miikka

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.740
We had a big punishment for the loser

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:49.440
Which was

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.100
For me it was to shave my head

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.160
And for Otto  it was to shave his beard

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.160
I have to say I was

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.180
I was rooting for Miikka

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.520
Just because I think it's worse to lose the hair

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.860
Than it's losing the beard

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.700
I have played Otto so many times

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.900
And this time it was just different

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.180
Miikka really likes to get nervous on those big matches

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:15.880
So I knew that I would not really have any huge problems beating him

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.260
What a shot!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.540
I have probably never been so nervous in a table tennis match in my whole life

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:24.960
I didn't want to lose my hair!

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.520
And I wanted to see Otto without a beard

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.720
That would have been fun

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.300
Of course

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:31.660
I won it

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.220
Pretty easily

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.540
But I just remembered one point

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.380
He somehow fell down on the floor

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.960
I have never seen Otto

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.720
Move so fast

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.140
It was so funny to see

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.740
That it was serious business for him too that match!

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:54.240
You see that sometimes from me when I really fight

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.060
And didn't want to lose my beard

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.180
During the whole match

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:00.980
It felt like Otto was on top all the time

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.660
Miikka just didn't have

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:03.940
Any chance

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:06.320
He was so scared to lose his hair

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.000
So I got my head shaved off

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.700
Looks pretty nice!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.480
Yeah free haircut!

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.280
One of the many cool ideas we have got

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.100
Was the synchronized table tennis

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.800
I think that's one of the
coolest videos

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.340
That we have actually done on our channel

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.500
Something that we had never seen
before

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.740
and never tried before

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.380
That's actually one of the most interesting
things about doing these videos

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.920
is getting to try stuff that's never been
tried before

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.920
And not knowing how it's going to work

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.760
This synchronized table tennis was one of those things

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:01.060
It's one of those videos that we thought
would be super cool

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.260
For the audience to watch

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.540
But it just didn't turn out so popular

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.100
In addition to this sync

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.180
One of the videos that we thought would do really well

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:12.660
Was the bubble bursting video

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.260
That was again super cool to make

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:19.960
But for some reason it wasn't so popular

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:21.920
And then on the other hand

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.680
There are those
videos that we think that:

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.440
"This is not even worth publishing"

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.870
And then that gets like millions of views

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:30.440
So you never really know for sure

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.800
What's a good video

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.800
At 600K we did triangular table tennis

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.200
The triangular table tennis

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.360
Is one of those examples that

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:46.160
We were thinking that should we even publish this video

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.300
We had messed up the microphones

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.840
so the audio quality was really bad

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:54.120
And I think it has maybe a couple of million views

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:55.800
Up to date

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.300
Yeah... that was interesting

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.360
And I think that also proves that

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.920
it's good to sometimes try out some new stuff on the channel

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.500
Because it might do well

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.540
And even start a series for the channel

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.340
Then we hit 700k subscribers

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:17.840
And the lake ping pong was quite a big project

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:20.140
By far one of the funniest projects we have
done

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.540
It was first of all super cool

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:29.060
But it was super difficult also to arrange

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:31.520
We spent there actually one week

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:35.640
The amount of time it took to film
one trick shot on the lake

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.240
It was so much longer than a normal trick shot because

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:39.620
We had the sun

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.620
it was always shining from the wrong direction

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.640
Now the sun is coming...

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.080
So you couldn't see anything

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.420
And then we had the wind

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.120
We have to wait a bit for the wind

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.520
So here we are

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:55.460
on a lake

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.200
waiting for the wind to blow away

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:00.020
Because if there is even a bit of wind

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:01.140
in the middle of the lake

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.780
There is no possibility to actually play there

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.800
It's just Emil's back spin - it's so strong!

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:13.500
We had the raft drifting away all the time

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.700
We had to get it to the same spot again

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.760
We had one camera on a boat

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.160
and the wind was blowing the boat this direction

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.440
the raft this direction

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.660
It was just...

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.080
Yeah it's blowing you away

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:26.440
Don't go!

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:30.580
We kept on having to go pick up the balls from the lake

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:35.400
There were so many things that were just
doing it very difficult for us to film the video

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.720
Now the floor is slippery!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.100
Luckily we had our friend Patrick helping us out

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.940
It was really really cool

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:46.500
When we were able to play in the middle of the lake

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:47.620
That was so much fun

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.019
We did a lot of filming

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.240
And then we had a sauna every night

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.700
We had a lot of fun at the cottage that week

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.280
Super cool project

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.000
Really happy that we made it!

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:59.980
Then we hit 800K

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.620
And then we made the 2 vs 1 on giant table

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.320
We thought if me and Emil both play at the same time

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.300
against Otto

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:08.920
Then we're gonna have a chance to win

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.160
I would like to say that

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.160
That I was sure that I'm going to beat them

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.560
But to be honest

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.260
I really thought that I would lose that one

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:18.920
Going in to that match

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:22.320
I didn't believe that Otto would have any chance

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.000
To win that match against me and Miikka

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:27.660
But how wrong can a person be...

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:30.300
We didn't have any chance

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:33.674
We thought it would be like a crazy advantage to have
two against one

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.860
But it ended up we just messing each other up

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.880
Otto was just playing to the middle

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.660
And neither of us knew who would take the ball

